{
  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-couchdb-2026-90800",
  "summary": "Apache CouchDB: Auth bypass in prefixed _users and _replicator databases",
  "details": "Missing authorisation checks in chttpd in Apache CouchDB 3.5.2 and below on all platforms allows any request to read the full contents of a prefixed _user or _replicator database via an unauthorised API endpoint.\n\n\nThe use of prefixed system databases is very rare.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 3.5.3, which fixes this issue.",
